# Prettier already skips node_modules and everything in .gitignore, so build output
# (.nuxt, .output, .data) needs no entry here. This file is for content that is tracked
# but is not ours to format.

# Vendored agent skills, one mirror per harness. They are synced from upstream repos and
# content-hashed in skills-lock.json: reformatting them changes the hash, and the next sync
# reverts the change anyway. 610 of the 737 files `prettier .` wanted to rewrite were these.
.agents/skills/
.claude/skills/
.opencode/skills/
.pi/skills/

# shadcn-vue CLI output. eslint.config.mjs exempts the same directory on the grounds that
# regenerating reproduces the file as it stands, which is exactly why formatting it is a trap:
# the next `shadcn-vue add` would diff against a layout the CLI never produces. Files edited by
# hand here are still written in this repo's style, they are just not machine-checked.
app/components/ui/

# Generated by their own tools, which rewrite them in their own layout. drizzle-kit owns the
# migration snapshots, and CLAUDE.md rule 5 forbids hand-editing anything under migrations at all.
pnpm-lock.yaml
skills-lock.json
server/db/migrations/
